        <body>
            <div xml:id="d348">

                <pb facs="0405" n="1239" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1239"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 658.119/390</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Chargé in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Laughlin</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Extract]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-05-29T20:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 29, 1918, 8 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>8008. For Sheldon [from
                    War Trade Board]:</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <p>Your 645, Embassy 10235, May 23, 8 p.m. You may include in letter of adhesion the
                    following relative to bunkering: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>The War Trade Board during the currency of the above-mentioned agreement
                            will grant bunker licenses freely tor coal and oil and stores for
                            Swedish vessels operating as contemplated by the agreement.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>We suggest a clause in this connection requiring that there would be no lay-up of
                    Swedish steamers during the currency of the agreement.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
